---
// How to get the salvage command. This is the one place on the site that says
// how to install it: when there's a release, change it here (and in the
// README's "Get it" section). Releases are per tool; this command's are
// tagged cli-v*.
---
<section class="get" aria-labelledby="get-salvage">
  <h2 id="get-salvage">Get it</h2>
  <p>
    There's no release yet, so you build <code>salvage</code> from source. You need Git and a stable Rust toolchain
    (<a href="https://rustup.rs">rustup.rs</a> installs one). Building takes a minute or two the first time.
  </p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Chapterists/salvage.git
cd salvage
cargo install --locked --path crates/salvage</code></pre>
  <p>
    That puts <code>salvage</code> in <code>~/.cargo/bin</code>. To try it without installing, run it from the
    repository with <code>cargo run -p salvage -- doctor</code>. To remove it, run <code>salvage lldb uninstall</code> if you installed the debugger formatters, then <code>cargo uninstall salvage</code>.
  </p>
</section>
